  "question": {
    "text": "A square loop is carrying a steady current <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> and the magnitude of its magnetic dipole moment is <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . If this square loop is changed to a circular loop and it carries the same current, the magnitude of the magnetic dipole moment of circular loop will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the side of square loop be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>.<br />The magnetic dipole is<math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br />Radius of circular loop <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> related to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&nbsp;as circumference of circular loop is equal to perimeter of square loop.<br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> New dipole moment <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>"
  }
}